---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Manifesto — JopChi"
  description="JopChi is not built to compete for every moment of your attention. Twice a day a rift opens: two hidden words, seven guesses, one decisive split."
>
  <article class="manifesto" aria-labelledby="manifesto-heading">
    <p class="section-label">Manifesto</p>
    <h1 id="manifesto-heading">
      <span class="gradient-text">The JopChi Manifesto</span>
    </h1>

    <div class="manifesto-body">
      <p class="lead">
        JopChi is not built to compete for every moment of your attention.
      </p>
      <p>
        Twice a day, a rift opens. Two words are hidden within it. You have
        seven guesses and one decisive split to reveal them both and close the
        rift.
      </p>
      <p class="beat">Then the board becomes still.</p>
      <p>
        There are no endless levels demanding to be completed, no season to keep
        up with and no pressure to turn a quiet achievement into a public
        performance. JopChi keeps your record, but leaves you in control of what
        it means and whether you share it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Beneath every puzzle is an original musical score created to make those
        few minutes feel distinct. It is not background noise or a soundtrack
        competing for attention. It is a changing atmosphere&mdash;present
        enough to give the puzzle character, yet restrained enough to leave room
        to think. It arrives with the rift and leaves when you do.
      </p>
      <p>
        JopChi lives comfortably on the screen in your pocket. It is patient
        about signing in, respectful of your time and ready for two brief
        appointments each day.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is also designed from the beginning for the many different ways
        people see, hear, move, read and play. Color supports the experience,
        but never carries essential meaning alone. Text can grow. Motion can be
        reduced. Contrast can be strengthened. Sound, touch, keyboard and switch
        controls can offer different paths across the same board.
      </p>
      <p>
        Accessibility is not an extra feature added after the game is finished.
        It is part of how JopChi is made. Our ambition is to create a word game
        worthy of recognition for inclusive design&mdash;not because everyone
        plays in the same way, but because everyone deserves an equally
        thoughtful way to play.
      </p>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="manifesto-pull">
      <p>
        If modern software often feels like a floodlight, JopChi is a lamp you
        aim for yourself.
      </p>
    </blockquote>

    <div class="manifesto-coda">
      <p>It does not ask to own your day.</p>
      <p>
        It asks for a few thoughtful minutes&mdash;and makes them count.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section aria-labelledby="offers-heading">
      <h2 id="offers-heading">What JopChi offers</h2>
      <ul class="offers-list" role="list">
        <li class="card">
          <strong>Two daily games</strong>&mdash;morning and evening&mdash;with
          two hidden words in each.
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <strong>Seven guesses, one split</strong> and a challenge that rewards
          insight rather than endless play.
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <strong>A personal record</strong> that waits quietly until you choose
          to view it.
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <strong>Accessible ways to play</strong> through sound, touch,
          keyboard, switch controls and reduced motion.
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <strong>Adjustable text, contrast and color palettes</strong> that
          adapt to the player.
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <strong>An original soundtrack</strong> designed to make a daily word
          puzzle feel like a small ritual.
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <strong>Complete freedom to share your result</strong>&mdash;or let
          the experience end exactly where it began.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="manifesto-footer-note">
      Curious how the accessibility claims are actually implemented? <a href="/accessibility">Read the accessibility page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .manifesto { max-width: 46rem; }

  .manifesto h1 {
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  /* Slightly larger, looser measure — this page is meant to be read, not scanned */
  .manifesto-body {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .manifesto-body p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    /* Avoid single-word last lines in long prose */
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* The opening line states the whole argument — given weight rather than a
     drop cap, which would split the word it starts with. */
  .manifesto-body .lead {
    font-size: 1.3125rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* A one-line paragraph that is meant to land as a pause, not a sentence
     swallowed into the paragraph above it. */
  .manifesto-body .beat {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .manifesto-pull {
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    padding: 1.75rem 2rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-bg-surface);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0;
  }

  .manifesto-pull p {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw + 0.75rem, 1.625rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* Closing couplet: two short lines that carry the ending */
  .manifesto-coda {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .manifesto-coda p {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .manifesto-coda p:last-child {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .manifesto section { margin-top: 3rem; }

  .offers-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .offers-list li {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .offers-list strong { color: var(--color-accent); }

  .manifesto-footer-note {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .manifesto h1 { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }

    /* Tighter leading and a smaller lead-in: at this measure the desktop
       values gave an overlong opening block. Each size has to be restated
       here — the class rules out-specify .manifesto-body on their own. */
    .manifesto-body { font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; }
    .manifesto-body .lead { font-size: 1.1875rem; }
    .manifesto-body .beat { font-size: 1.125rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
    .manifesto-body p { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }

    .manifesto-pull { margin: 2rem 0; padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem; }
    .manifesto-coda { margin-top: 2rem; }
    .manifesto-coda p { font-size: 1.0625rem; }
    .manifesto section { margin-top: 2.25rem; }
    .offers-list li { padding: 1rem 1.125rem; }
    .manifesto-footer-note { margin-top: 2.25rem; }
  }
</style>
